# Gaggimate baseline commits

Use these when the user asks how something worked **originally**, **in upstream**, **before our changes**, **before the fork**, or similar.

Full reference: [docs/baseline-commits.md](../../docs/baseline-commits.md)

## Fixed baselines

| Name | Commit | Git ref (if tagged) | Meaning |
|------|--------|---------------------|---------|
| **upstream-original** | `69ce0c003279` | `upstream-original` | **Gaggimate original code** — tree at `git clone git@github.com:jniebuhr/gaggimate.git` (May 2026). Compare here for true upstream behavior. |
| **upstream-remote** | (moving) | `upstream/master` | Current upstream `master`; run `git fetch upstream` first. |

## Fork baselines (moving)

| Name | Ref | Meaning |
|------|-----|---------|
| **fork-published** | `origin/master` | Latest commit pushed to `git@github.com:phamhanh/gaggimate.git`. Run `git fetch origin` first. |
| **fork-head** | `HEAD` | Latest local commit (may be unpushed). |
| **working-tree** | (uncommitted) | Changes on disk not yet in `fork-head`. |

## How to interpret user wording

| User says | Default baseline | Compare with |
|-----------|------------------|--------------|
| originally, original Gaggimate, upstream, stock, at clone | **upstream-original** (`69ce0c00`) | current file or `fork-head` |
| before our fork / since I forked (whole repo) | **upstream-original** | `fork-head` or path |
| before our changes (single feature, this repo) | **upstream-original** unless context is clearly only recent work | `fork-head` or working-tree |
| before the last commit / before I committed X | `HEAD~1` or named commit | `fork-head` |
| before what's on GitHub / before I pushed | **fork-published** | `fork-head` |
| before this chat / this session | Not stored reliably; use **fork-head** + `git diff` / `git status`, or ask | working-tree |

If ambiguous between **upstream-original** and **fork-published**, prefer **upstream-original** for "original" and **fork-published** for "what I last shipped."

## Commands (prefer these)

```bash
# File at upstream-original
git show 69ce0c00:path/to/file

# Diff one file vs upstream-original
git diff 69ce0c00 -- path/to/file

# Diff whole tree vs upstream-original
git diff 69ce0c00

# Same if local tag exists
git diff upstream-original -- path/to/file
```

When explaining behavior, cite both the baseline name and the short hash (`69ce0c00`).

## Clone commands (reference)

```bash
# Upstream (original project) — baseline commit above
git clone git@github.com:jniebuhr/gaggimate.git

# This fork (OTA / Iberital Express)
git clone git@github.com:phamhanh/gaggimate.git
```

Remotes in this workspace: `origin` → phamhanh fork, `upstream` → jniebuhr (fetch only).
